          content: [
            `The story unfolds across the sprawling reaches of the Tacoune Archipelago — a bustling crossroads of the world’s maritime trade routes, resting at the very heart of the White Sea.`,
            `Look out upon the White Sea — why is it called that?`,
            `Across the shimmering azure water, countless white seagulls wheel and soar through the boundless sky, their wings dipping toward vast, silvery-white beaches stretching along every coast of this great archipelago. This is Tacoune, the largest island nation in all the world.`,
            `The gulls glide high on ocean thermals before diving sharply downward, skimming over sun-drenched hills and sleepy inland villages, sweeping over open-air markets rich with the briny scent of fresh seafood, over deep harbors packed with merchant vessels... until they alight upon the weathered tiled roofs of Noha Town.`,
            `Down near the docks, the rhythmic clink of wrenches echoed from an open repair shed.`,
            `"Hey, Berch! Isn't today the day your wife’s giving birth? What in the world are you still doing crouched over an engine?"`,
            `The engineer wiping grease and sweat from his brow let out an easy laugh, not looking up from the exposed gears. "Oh, she’s already finished up at the clinic. There's nothing left for an old grease-monkey like me to do there right now."`,
            `The mechanic blinked in disbelief, then burst into a wide grin, clapping his hands together. "Ha! Well congratulations, man! So—what did you catch? A seagull or a big fish?"`,
            `A few nearby dockworkers paused their work and chuckled. One called out from across the floor, "Yeah, don't hold out on us, Berch! Which one is it?"`,
            `Berch tightened the final bolt with a practiced flick of his wrist. Looking up with a wry half-smile, he tried to sound casual. "Seagull or big fish... makes no difference to me."`,
            `"Come on, be serious!" The mechanic laughed, giving Berch a hearty slap on the shoulder. "You two have been praying for a child for years. You can't just shrug it off like you're tuning an old turbine!"`,
            `Berch smiled softly, wiping the black engine oil from his calloused palms onto a rag. His gaze drifted to the humming generator he had just brought back to life, his voice dropping to a quiet, tender murmur:`,
            `"...It's a seagull."`,
            `* * *`,
            `In Tacoune, people share an old coastal saying: "A son is a seagull; a daughter is a big fish."`,
            `It stems from an ancient seafaring belief — that sons will one day spread their wings and fly away across the vast horizons to seek their fortunes, whereas daughters remain rooted to the islands, tending the hearth and keeping the family lineage alive. That is why, to many islanders in Tacoune, welcoming a daughter is treasured like landing a prize catch that never leaves their native waters. Raising a son, meanwhile, is like nurturing a fledgling seagull — one knows from the very first day that when the wind turns, he will soar toward distant shores.`
          ],
