          content: [
            `"Are you absolutely certain you passed? Don't tell me all those hours I spent drilling calculus into your thick skull went to waste!"`,
            `Mizz strolled barefoot along the water's edge, her hands clasped behind her back as the gentle surf lapped against her ankles.`,
            `Beside her, Koralh took a deep, invigorating breath of the morning sea air, a triumphant grin spreading across his face. He sat down upon the warm sand, patting the space beside him.`,
            `"Passed with top honors in mechanical sciences, thank you very much! My admission to Cetoriwart University in Siranious is officially secured. Hyzo and I will be in the same collegiate department."`,
            `Mizz lowered herself gracefully onto the sand beside him, pulling her knees to her chest. "Hyzo... that's your childhood friend, right?"`,
            `"Yeah," Koralh nodded, his gaze drifting out across the blue expanse. "He's the one who filed my deferment while I was lost. Ever since we were five years old, even though he often seemed distant and walled off from the world, he never once turned his back on me. In a lot of ways... I've always felt like he was someone walking miles ahead of his time."`,
            `Mizz watched his profile, her lips curving into a soft, teasing smile. "He’s the only friend you ever talk about. If he’s your first friend... does that make me your second?"`,
            `Koralh turned his head, his hazel eyes locking with hers beneath the radiant morning sun. Reaching down, his fingers gently intertwined with hers on the sand.`,
            `"It's completely different with you, Mizz..." Koralh murmured, his voice rich with honest tenderness. "You're in a category all your own... something far deeper than mere friendship."`,
            `Mizz’s breath hitched. A delicate blush bloomed across her cheeks, yet she didn't pull her hand away. Slowly, gently, she leaned her head against his shoulder, letting the rhythmic hush of the waves envelop them in peace.`,
            `"You've only known me a few weeks, Koralh Berch," she whispered softly. "And already you talk like a veteran poet."`,
            `Koralh laughed warmly, pointing toward the promontory. "Come on. There's one last place I want to show you before we leave."`,
            `Hand in hand, they climbed the stone path leading up to the Old BlackLighthouse, ascending the rusted spiral staircase until they emerged onto the wind-whipped observation balcony.`,
            `High above the cliffs, the ocean stretched boundlessly in every direction.`,
            `"Look over there," Mizz pointed toward the distant northern horizon, where a majestic, mountainous landmass rose through the sea haze like a slumbering giant. "That’s the southern coast of Siranious."`,
            `"It looks immense," Koralh whispered, leaning against the iron railing. "I used to take naps up here when I felt lost. The harbor down there always looks so frantic and chaotic, but from up here... everything feels so still."`,
            `Mizz turned to him, the coastal wind tossing her chestnut hair across her face. "You'll be setting foot on that mainland in two days, Koralh. Our hold is nearly packed, and the tide turns at dawn on the first of May."`,
            `Koralh nodded, his eyes fixed firmly upon the distant continent. "I'm ready."`,
            `* * *`,
            `The evening before departure, the Berch dining room was unusually hushed.`,
            `The lively chatter that typically filled the house was replaced by the clink of silverware and the unspoken weight of approaching separation.`,
            `"Is your trunk completely packed, Koralh?" Mrs. Berch asked softly, keeping her eyes on her plate.`,
            `"Yes, Mom," Koralh answered gently. "Everything is ready."`,
            `After dinner, Koralh returned to his bedroom to make his final preparations. Standing before his desk, his gaze lingered upon the thick lead-lined glass jar holding the BlackMirror shard. Tucking it deep into his inner travel coat alongside the Ivelf lexicon, he locked his leather satchel.`,
            `The next morning at dawn, the house buzzed with hurried activity.`,
            `Mrs. Berch practically filled his arms with packages of fresh-baked sweet pastries, smoked fish, and warm wool blankets.`,
            `"Take these for the voyage, my sweet boy! Eat well! Keep yourself warm! Write to us every week!" Her voice cracked as tears spilled down her cheeks.`,
            `"Mom, please, I'll be fine," Koralh said, embracing her tightly with all the love in his heart.`,
            `Stepping forward, Mr. Berch pressed a thick roll of imperial banknotes into his son's palm.`,
            `"Take this for your campus housing and travel expenses," the engineer said, his voice steady yet thick with emotion. "Things on the mainland are fast and expensive. Don't hesitate to ask if you need more."`,
            `Gathering his luggage, Koralh paused at the front gate, looking back at his parents standing beneath the morning sun — his mother waving tearfully, his father standing tall with his arm wrapped around her shoulders, squinting through unshed tears as the coastal breeze ruffled their hair.`,
            `"I'm off, Mom, Dad!" Koralh called out, waving with a radiant, confident smile. "Don't worry about me — your seagull knows how to fly!"`,
            `Stepping into the coastal cab, Koralh watched Noha Town recede through the glass.`,
            `The cobblestone streets, the bustling fish stalls, the familiar schoolyard, the old lighthouse standing guard upon the dunes — all slipped past like the pages of a cherished book reaching its close.`,
            `Closing his eyes as the cab approached the harbor wharves, Koralh took a deep, steadying breath, his heart beating with fierce anticipation for the vast, uncharted horizon awaiting him across the White Sea.`,
            `* * *`,
            `The Everbranch`,
            `The Great Tree has endured since the first dawn of the cosmos, its colossal roots anchored deep within the molten core of the living earth, sheltering entire hidden ecosystems within its vast, subterranean expanse.`,
            `The foliage of the Everbranch is forged not of mortal wood, but of shimmering, crystalline mirrors — and those crystal leaves are far more than mere ornamentation: each radiant facet reflects an entire branching reality of the multiverse.`,
            `In the primordial era, the winged race known as the Ivelf were consecrated by The Mother, entrusted with the sacred covenant of guarding every single crystal leaf upon the boughs.`,
            `For should those fragile mirrors ever fall and shatter... the multiverse shall be stripped of all possibility, doomed to march down a single, inescapable path toward absolute annihilation.`
          ],
